  "sourceDecisions": [
    "Historical Damh lordships remain despite war and partial occupation. Eoghainn asylum and Forsyth additional placement remain.",
    "Four Eoghainn gaps, two Oglivy gaps and one in each remaining diagram; no invented founder years or current heads.",
    "Agnew Glaodhaich/Seallach/Quíghleann descend from Loinneog–Zachair. Elid Xubhnán/Xarthan/Zibhí descend from Zeargán and the unnamed spouse.",
    "Eanbharr was 14 at Seallachs source birth; Vadria was 15 at Poilíns birth from the confirmed forced relationship. Explicit source years are retained.",
    "Pádraig the undated founder is explicitly distinct from Pádraig (*1714). Founder house affiliations and cross-diagram aliases are reviewed.",
    "Eleven outgoing wards retain biological parentage. Incoming Uisigh has one foster record containing both guardians, with no invented biological parents.",
    "Known counterpart birth/death years and canonical names supplement lower-information graphic readings. Muircheartach Casur 1604, Koarnach Culloch 1610, Mairghread Ness 1613 and Heilbhic Muirgheal 1657 follow their origin tables.",
    "Dated Agnew evidence supersedes authorized reconstructed Banlaoch births, preserving established IDs and historical source notes. Glaodhaich (*1700) receives his formerly unknown birth and living status in Luthsach.",
    "Existing relationship status is retained where diagrams supply no new evidence. No unrelated pair statuses are normalized.",
    "No portraits or warrior illustrations were supplied. Existing canonical portraits are reused; missing portraits and crests remain placeholders. No unregistered house or guardian is fabricated for Laga, Kerlaouen or Marcaigh."
  ],
